# known-legit matches (regex per line)
# placeholder volume names: convention is that examples start with "Your"
/Volumes/Your[A-Za-z0-9]*
# standard commit trailers carry an email by design
^\s*(Co-Authored-By|Signed-off-by|Reviewed-by|Thanks-to|Acked-by):
# the scanner's own rules table (it contains the patterns it hunts for)
^\s*(home-path|named-volume|camera-filename|credential-assignment|key-format|private-key-block|secret-file-path|email)\|
# the strict-seal driver READS the stock Claude Code config filename at runtime
# (server definitions; credentials are never written to the tree — filename alone leaks nothing)
\.claude\.json
